AC3: Authenticated admin (admin@admin.com) posts an arbitrary/attacker
topic — must always resolve to admin_message.

Login: POST /login_submit (role=admin, real session/captcha flow) -> 302
  to /admin (authenticated session cookie established).

Request:
  POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/subscribeToTopic
    -H "X-XSRF-TOKEN: <admin session XSRF>"
    -d "token=admin-live-test-token"
    -d "topic=store_panel_999_message"

Response:
  HTTP/1.1 200 OK
  {"message":"Successfully subscribed to topic"}

Code (unconditional, no request-input dependence):
  $topic = auth('admin')->check() ? 'admin_message' : 'store_panel_'...
Combined with the mocked backstop test
(test_authenticated_admin_always_gets_admin_message_topic, posts
topic=store_panel_{7}_message, asserts subscribeToTopic() called with
literal 'admin_message') — full proof the posted value never matters
for an admin session.
